{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Thank you for being a friend
[Eb]Traveled down a road and back again
Your [F]heart is true, you're a pal and a [Bb]confidant
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]I'm not ashamed to say
[Eb]I hope it always will stay this way
My [F]hat is off, won’t you stand up and take a [Bb]bow[Bb][F][Gm]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm]And if you threw a [Bb7]party [Eb]Invited everyone you [D7]knew
Well, [Fm]you would [Bb7]see The biggest [Cm7]gift would be from [Gm]me
And the [Eb]card attached would [F]say
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Thank you for being a [Bb]friend Thank you for being a [Eb]friend
[Eb]Thank you for being a [F]friend Thank you for being a [Bb]friend
Bb     Eb   (with riff)
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
If it’s a car you lack
I’d surely buy you a Cadillac
Whatever you need any time of the day or night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
I'm not ashamed to say
I hope it always will stay this way
My hat is off, won't you stand up and take a bow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
And when we both get older With walking canes and hair of gray
Have no fear Even though it's hardly here
I will stand real close and say
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And when we [Fm]die, and float [Gm]away
Into the [Ebm]night, the milky [Bb]way
You'll hear me [Fm]call as we [Gm]ascend
I'll say your [Ebm]name then once [Bb]again
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
Thank you for being a friend
Bb                       Eb  With riffs and Bah ba ba ba Bah ba ba
{end_of_verse}
